WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.833 --> 00:00:01.835 line:0%
-That's my favorite song.

00:00:01.835 --> 00:00:02.969 line:0%
Guys, welcome to

00:00:02.969 --> 00:00:04.837 line:0%
"The Tonight Show:
At Home Edition."

00:00:04.837 --> 00:00:06.206 line:0%
My name is Jimmy Fallon.

00:00:06.206 --> 00:00:08.441
Thank you so much
for tuning in to our shows.

00:00:08.441 --> 00:00:09.842
We're trying to give you

00:00:09.842 --> 00:00:12.479
a fresh hour of entertainment
every single night.

00:00:12.479 --> 00:00:17.250
It's been pretty grim news,
every single day,

00:00:17.250 --> 00:00:19.852
but today was a little glimmer
of hope in New York City

00:00:19.852 --> 00:00:22.688
that we may have
flattened the curve,

00:00:22.688 --> 00:00:24.457
which is, you know,
far from over,

00:00:24.457 --> 00:00:26.592
but, any good news, I'll take.

00:00:26.592 --> 00:00:29.228
And I think that's awesome,
that we're all staying at home.

00:00:29.228 --> 00:00:30.463
It's working.

00:00:30.463 --> 00:00:32.031
So, everyone staying at home,
thank you so much

00:00:32.031 --> 00:00:33.999
for doing that.

00:00:33.999 --> 00:00:35.234
It is doing something,

00:00:35.234 --> 00:00:37.670
so, I applaud every one
of you for doing that.

00:00:37.670 --> 00:00:39.205
I know how hard it can be.

00:00:39.205 --> 00:00:42.008
I'm very lucky to have
this house and this family,

00:00:42.008 --> 00:00:44.076
but, it's tough,
so, I applaud you guys.

00:00:44.076 --> 00:00:45.878
Thank you for staying at home.

00:00:45.878 --> 00:00:47.613
Let's flatten that curve.

00:00:47.613 --> 00:00:49.449
We have a great show tonight.

00:00:49.449 --> 00:00:50.916
Kerry Washington is on the show.

00:00:50.916 --> 00:00:52.651
She's a good friend of our show

00:00:52.651 --> 00:00:55.087
and she has a new show called
"Little Fires Everywhere,"

00:00:55.087 --> 00:00:58.558
that her and Reese Witherspoon
are starring in on Hulu.

00:00:58.558 --> 00:01:00.092
And get those two together,
I'm there.

00:01:00.092 --> 00:01:01.794
I'll watch that show anytime.

00:01:01.794 --> 00:01:06.099 line:0%
Her charity is...

00:01:06.099 --> 00:01:07.834 line:0%
and we thank Kerry
for coming on.

00:01:07.834 --> 00:01:09.201 line:0%
We'll be talking to her
later in the show.

00:01:09.201 --> 00:01:12.538 line:0%
Also, Andrew Rannells,
from the show "Black Monday,"

00:01:12.538 --> 00:01:14.840
will be on the show.
On Showtime.

00:01:14.840 --> 00:01:17.743 line:0%
Andrew, he was supposed
to be our show Friday,

00:01:17.743 --> 00:01:20.212 line:0%
before we left the studio.

00:01:20.212 --> 00:01:22.915 line:0%
His charity is Meal Train.

00:01:22.915 --> 00:01:23.950 line:0%
I've never heard of this.

00:01:23.950 --> 00:01:25.718 line:0%
This is a new charity to me,

00:01:25.718 --> 00:01:27.153 line:0%
but it's fascinating,
how they're

00:01:27.153 --> 00:01:29.822 line:0%
feeding people that are
on the front line.

00:01:29.822 --> 00:01:31.056 line:0%
It's a really cool way to do it

00:01:31.056 --> 00:01:33.025 line:0%
and I think kind of
an unknown charity,

00:01:33.025 --> 00:01:34.960 line:0%
so that's a great thing

00:01:34.960 --> 00:01:37.263 line:0%
to broadcast
to millions of people

00:01:37.263 --> 00:01:40.032 line:0%
watching our show
on NBC and on YouTube,

00:01:40.032 --> 00:01:42.168 line:0%
so thank you so much.

00:01:42.168 --> 00:01:43.836 line:0%
Click on that
and donate to that.

00:01:43.836 --> 00:01:45.504 line:0%
Very cool.
Then, we're closing out the show

00:01:45.504 --> 00:01:48.507 line:0%
with Anderson Paak [ Clap ]
and the Free Nationals!

00:01:48.507 --> 00:01:50.577
Anderson Paak!
He has a song

00:01:50.577 --> 00:01:52.645
in the new
"Trolls World Tour" movie,

00:01:52.645 --> 00:01:54.113
[ Shouting in distance ]
which is out today.

00:01:54.113 --> 00:01:55.815
Right now,
you can get it On Demand.

00:01:55.815 --> 00:01:59.419
Go to -- Well,
"'Trolls' movie" --

00:01:59.419 --> 00:02:01.020
I don't know.
Google "Trolls."

00:02:01.020 --> 00:02:02.989
How do I watch
the "Trolls" movie?

00:02:02.989 --> 00:02:04.591
-I don't know,
but we will be watching it.

00:02:04.591 --> 00:02:06.693
-I know we'll -- more than once.

00:02:06.693 --> 00:02:08.894
Really? You don't wanna hear
"Mary Had a Little Lamb"

00:02:08.894 --> 00:02:10.763
150 times?
-But we can do all.

00:02:10.763 --> 00:02:11.964
-We can do all.
-We've got time for all of it.

00:02:11.964 --> 00:02:13.399
-Uh-oh, what's --
Oh, no.

00:02:13.399 --> 00:02:16.669
You know I don't like one
animal, and one animal only.

00:02:16.669 --> 00:02:17.903
Oh!
-Uh-oh.

00:02:17.903 --> 00:02:20.106
-My goodness!
What is this?

00:02:20.106 --> 00:02:22.075
-[ Hissing ]
-What sounds like that?

00:02:22.075 --> 00:02:23.442
-[ Hisses ]

00:02:23.442 --> 00:02:25.445
-Sna-a-a-a-a-a-a-ke!

00:02:25.445 --> 00:02:26.512
[ Laughing ]
Oh, no!

00:02:26.512 --> 00:02:28.547
Get that snake away from me.

00:02:28.547 --> 00:02:31.117
Aaaaah! Aaaaah!

00:02:31.117 --> 00:02:32.919
I'm so scared of the snake.
-Ahhhhh!

00:02:32.919 --> 00:02:34.186
-Thank you so --
Oh, no.

00:02:34.186 --> 00:02:35.855
Get that snake --
I'm afraid of the snake.

00:02:35.855 --> 00:02:38.391
I'm afraid of paper cuts, too.

00:02:38.391 --> 00:02:41.861 line:0%
I will say that
Anderson Paak's charity...

00:02:41.861 --> 00:02:44.464 line:0%
-Winnie, I wanna play that, too.
-...That he is doing is...

00:02:46.899 --> 00:02:50.469 line:0%
...which is raising money,
'cause a lot of the crews

00:02:50.469 --> 00:02:52.004 line:0%
that are part
of these giant tours

00:02:52.004 --> 00:02:54.706 line:0%
and theses concerts are
out of jobs as well.

00:02:54.706 --> 00:02:57.744
And unemployment, honestly,
is at an all-time high.

00:02:57.744 --> 00:03:01.113
I don't know --
I mean, this is my crew,

00:03:01.113 --> 00:03:02.515
so I don't know what I'd do
without my wife.

00:03:02.515 --> 00:03:03.749
Thank you, honey.
-[ Chuckle ]

00:03:03.749 --> 00:03:06.418
-And, Winnie and Frannie,
thank you guys so much.

00:03:06.418 --> 00:03:08.454
Again, Frannie,
one of your best,

00:03:08.454 --> 00:03:09.889 line:0%
one of your best works.

00:03:09.889 --> 00:03:13.125 line:0%
I think, around here is where
you just thought about,

00:03:13.125 --> 00:03:16.629 line:0%
you know,
playing something else.

00:03:16.629 --> 00:03:17.629
But it's Friday.

00:03:17.629 --> 00:03:19.398
Let's go do some
monologue jokes.

00:03:19.398 --> 00:03:21.534
♪♪

00:03:21.534 --> 00:03:23.135 line:0%
You wanna get up?
[ Tapping ]

00:03:23.135 --> 00:03:25.404 line:0%
[ Patting thighs ]
Come up! Up!

00:03:25.404 --> 00:03:26.572 line:0%
Up!

00:03:26.639 --> 00:03:29.075 line:0%
Up.

00:03:29.075 --> 00:03:31.377 line:0%
Good girl. Up.

00:03:31.377 --> 00:03:33.145 line:0%
Up.

00:03:33.145 --> 00:03:34.246 line:0%
Good girl. Sit!

00:03:34.246 --> 00:03:35.248 line:0%
-[ Laughing ]

00:03:35.248 --> 00:03:37.116 line:0%
-Good girl! Sit!

00:03:37.116 --> 00:03:38.584 line:0%
-[ Laughing ]
-Good girl.

00:03:38.584 --> 00:03:40.553 line:0%
Gary.
-Just tell her to be cute.

00:03:40.553 --> 00:03:42.021 line:0%
-Alright. Be cute.

00:03:42.021 --> 00:03:45.791 line:0%
-Aww. She's such a good dog.
-[ Laughing ]

00:03:45.791 --> 00:03:47.960 line:0%
[ Sigh ]

00:03:47.960 --> 00:03:49.562 line:0%
Thank you, Gary.

00:03:49.562 --> 00:03:52.365 line:0%
Breathe! Breathe heavy.
-[ Laughing ]

00:03:52.365 --> 00:03:53.399 line:0%
-On my leg.

00:03:53.399 --> 00:03:55.168 line:0%
-[ Laughing intensifies ]
-Good girl. See?

00:03:55.168 --> 00:03:57.636 line:0%
We did a little trick
I taught her.
-"On my leg."

00:03:57.636 --> 00:04:00.740
-Not many dogs know
that one, huh?

00:04:00.740 --> 00:04:02.575
But you do, Gary.
You know it.

00:04:02.575 --> 00:04:04.410
-[ Laughing ]

00:04:04.410 --> 00:04:06.713
-[ Taps desk ]

00:04:06.713 --> 00:04:08.514
Yeah. Welcome
to "The Tonight Show:
At Home Edition."

00:04:08.514 --> 00:04:11.217
Well, you guys,
this Sunday is Easter.

00:04:11.217 --> 00:04:12.317
Happy Easter, everyone.

00:04:12.317 --> 00:04:13.486
You can tell everyone is trying

00:04:13.486 --> 00:04:14.554
to be safe for the holiday.

00:04:14.554 --> 00:04:16.222
Earlier today,
I saw the Easter bunny

00:04:16.222 --> 00:04:19.258
rubbing Purell
on his jelly beans.

00:04:19.258 --> 00:04:20.893
That's right, Easter is Sunday,

00:04:20.893 --> 00:04:23.663
and it's hard
to make things festive.

00:04:23.663 --> 00:04:25.965
We're really in trouble.
We don't even have

00:04:25.965 --> 00:04:28.133
the fake grass to put
in the Easter basket.

00:04:28.133 --> 00:04:30.569
After the show, I'm gonna have
to take a Kermit doll

00:04:30.569 --> 00:04:32.438
and crank him
through our pasta maker.

00:04:33.739 --> 00:04:35.908
[ Laughs ]

00:04:35.908 --> 00:04:37.543
That's right,
it's almost Easter

00:04:37.543 --> 00:04:39.612
and, even though everyone is
in quarantine, on Sunday,

00:04:39.612 --> 00:04:41.113
millions of parents
will be like,

00:04:41.113 --> 00:04:42.548
"Sweetie, I bought
you this dress

00:04:42.548 --> 00:04:44.584
and you're wearing it
for my Instagram post."

00:04:44.584 --> 00:04:45.685
-[ Laughs ]

00:04:47.486 --> 00:04:49.888
-Gotta get those likes.

00:04:49.888 --> 00:04:52.625
Let's get to some news.
Dr. Fauci says he expects

00:04:52.625 --> 00:04:56.329
that students will be able
to return to school in the fall,

00:04:56.329 --> 00:04:58.264
or, as homeschool
students put it,

00:04:58.264 --> 00:05:01.167
"Wow, that's just
40 months away."

00:05:04.570 --> 00:05:06.238
Listen to this --
In London, two people

00:05:06.238 --> 00:05:07.306
across the street
from each other

00:05:07.306 --> 00:05:10.042
performed "Romeo and Juliet"

00:05:10.042 --> 00:05:11.810
while their neighbors
kept yelling for them

00:05:11.810 --> 00:05:13.346
to both drink poison.

00:05:13.346 --> 00:05:15.914
[ Laughing ]

00:05:15.914 --> 00:05:19.352
[ English accent ]
It's 3:00 in the morning!

00:05:19.352 --> 00:05:21.553
A man in England spent
four days walking

00:05:21.553 --> 00:05:23.556
up the stairs in his house
until he ascended

00:05:23.556 --> 00:05:26.592
the height of Mount Everest,

00:05:26.592 --> 00:05:28.827
which just goes to show you,
anything is possible

00:05:28.827 --> 00:05:32.998
when you're avoiding
homeschooling your kids.

00:05:32.998 --> 00:05:34.567
And, finally,
there's a website called

00:05:34.567 --> 00:05:37.269
"Make Me a Cocktail"
that shows you how

00:05:37.269 --> 00:05:40.139
to make drinks with the
ingredients in your fridge,

00:05:40.139 --> 00:05:41.607
though, after a month
of quarantine,

00:05:41.607 --> 00:05:45.544
most people's only option
is a duck-sauce-tini.

00:05:45.544 --> 00:05:46.611
There you have it, everybody.

00:05:46.611 --> 00:05:48.447
That is my monologue!

00:05:48.447 --> 00:05:49.748
It is Friday and that's usually

00:05:49.748 --> 00:05:52.285
when I send out some emails,
I check on some stuff,

00:05:52.285 --> 00:05:55.054
and I usually some write
some thank-you notes.

00:05:55.054 --> 00:05:57.456
Let's do some thank-you notes
right now. Let's go.

00:05:57.456 --> 00:05:59.859
[ Funk sting plays ]

00:05:59.859 --> 00:06:02.094 line:0%
James, can I get some thank-you
note writing music, please?

00:06:02.094 --> 00:06:03.228 line:0%
♪♪

00:06:03.228 --> 00:06:04.830 line:0%
Perfect.

00:06:04.830 --> 00:06:07.800 line:0%
Thank you, Bernie Sanders,
for running such a principled

00:06:07.800 --> 00:06:10.169 line:0%
and inspiring
presidential campaign.

00:06:10.169 --> 00:06:12.038 line:0%
Tonight, treat yourself
to that whole bag

00:06:12.038 --> 00:06:13.339 line:0%
of Werther's Originals.

00:06:13.339 --> 00:06:14.406 line:0%
You've earned it.

00:06:14.406 --> 00:06:21.547 line:0%
♪♪

00:06:21.547 --> 00:06:24.517 line:0%
Thank you, recently released
"Coachella" documentary,

00:06:24.517 --> 00:06:27.953 line:0%
for making me feel nostalgic
about a woman in a flower crown

00:06:27.953 --> 00:06:30.222 line:0%
hugging me and then
vomiting on my back.

00:06:30.222 --> 00:06:33.792 line:0%
♪♪

00:06:33.792 --> 00:06:35.227 line:0%
We'll be back there soon, guys.

00:06:35.227 --> 00:06:37.596 line:0%
♪♪

00:06:37.596 --> 00:06:42.267 line:0%
Thank you, wearing face masks
when you leave your house,

00:06:42.267 --> 00:06:44.503 line:0%
for making every trip
to the grocery store feel like

00:06:44.503 --> 00:06:46.238 line:0%
"Mad Max: Fury Road."

00:06:46.238 --> 00:06:51.510 line:0%
♪♪

00:06:51.510 --> 00:06:53.779 line:0%
Thank you, quarantine,

00:06:53.779 --> 00:06:55.915 line:0%
for bringing out
the best in Americans --

00:06:55.915 --> 00:06:58.850 line:0%
our resilience, our acts
of support for one another,

00:06:58.850 --> 00:07:00.052 line:0%
and, for some reason,

00:07:00.052 --> 00:07:01.887 line:0%
an obscene amount
of banana bread.

00:07:01.887 --> 00:07:03.955 line:0%
♪♪

00:07:03.955 --> 00:07:05.157 line:0%
I'm on two loaves a week.

00:07:05.157 --> 00:07:10.729 line:0%
♪♪

00:07:10.729 --> 00:07:13.933 line:0%
Thank you, everybody
leaving a Zoom conference,

00:07:13.933 --> 00:07:15.401 line:0%
for giving me a brief moment

00:07:15.401 --> 00:07:18.770 line:0%
to see how all of my coworkers
are really feeling.

00:07:18.770 --> 00:07:19.872 line:0%
Bye, guys!

00:07:19.872 --> 00:07:28.580 line:0%
♪♪

00:07:28.580 --> 00:07:31.550 line:0%
Thank you,
changing your bedsheets,

00:07:31.550 --> 00:07:32.951 line:0%
or, as it's called now,

00:07:32.951 --> 00:07:34.153 line:0%
cleaning your office.

00:07:34.153 --> 00:07:39.959 line:0%
♪♪

00:07:39.959 --> 00:07:43.195 line:0%
Thank you,
not wanting to waste food,

00:07:43.195 --> 00:07:46.165 line:0%
for justifying last night's
onion-and-cookie dinner.

00:07:46.165 --> 00:07:53.172 line:0%
♪♪

00:07:53.172 --> 00:07:58.244 line:0%
♪♪

00:07:58.244 --> 00:08:00.879 line:0%
Thank you,
NASA researchers announcing

00:08:00.879 --> 00:08:04.116 line:0%
there's gas coming from Uranus.

00:08:04.116 --> 00:08:05.917 line:0%
Hm. Ooh.

00:08:05.917 --> 00:08:07.486 line:0%
If only there was a joke there.

00:08:07.486 --> 00:08:16.828 line:0%
♪♪

00:08:16.828 --> 00:08:19.231 line:0%
Thank you, bathrooms,

00:08:19.231 --> 00:08:21.233 line:0%
or, as parents with toddlers
call them now,

00:08:21.233 --> 00:08:22.468 line:0%
panic rooms.

00:08:22.468 --> 00:08:30.209 line:0%
♪♪

00:08:30.209 --> 00:08:33.045 line:0%
Thank you,
America staying home.

00:08:33.045 --> 00:08:34.246 line:0%
Even though we're apart,

00:08:34.246 --> 00:08:37.216 line:0%
we can come together
over one simple idea --

00:08:37.216 --> 00:08:40.152 line:0%
teachers should make
a billion dollars.

00:08:40.152 --> 00:08:41.487 line:0%
♪♪

00:08:41.487 --> 00:08:42.922 line:0%
Those are my thank-you notes.

00:08:42.922 --> 00:08:45.725 line:0%
We'll be right back with more
"Tonight Show: At Home Edition."

